X86_64 Spinlock2
(* Test-and-test-and-set spinlock on x86-TSO.
   Acquire: spin with plain loads until `lock` reads 0, then `xchg`
   (implicitly locked) 1 into it; if the old value was 1 go back to
   spinning. Critical section increments a shared counter. Release with a
   plain store (correct under TSO: a store is never reordered with the
   earlier loads and stores of the critical section).
   The read-spin matters for the explorer: a bare `xchg` loop writes a
   new message on every failed attempt, so the spinning thread's state
   never repeats and the exploration does not terminate.
   Two threads each increment once.
   Property: counter = 2 in every final state.
   Proved for every layout of the runner's image, the code verbatim
   (`decls = {}`): `SpinAbs.x64_spin_counter_envG_verbatim`
   (Promising/SLR/EnvG/X64SpinAbsPublic.lean). Proved from the runner's
   exact configuration (declarations and initial memory included):
   `SpinAbs.x64_spin_counter_envG_runner` (X64SpinAbsRunner.lean), with a
   `.Concrete` instance.
   Proved no fault at the runner's declarations (rule-level):
   `SpinAbs.x64_spin_counter_envG_runner_noFault`
   (Promising/SLR/EnvG/X64NoFaultDLocks.lean), with a `.Concrete` instance.
   With symbol operands as registers: `SpinPublicG.x64_spin_counter_envG`
   (Promising/SLR/EnvG/X64SpinPublicG.lean); pre-EnvG:
   `X64SpinInv.x64_counter_spin` (Promising/SLR/X64SpinFinalX.lean).
   The shared symbols are typed (`uint32_t`) so that the runner declares
   them as sized locations at the width of the code's accesses (DECLS): the
   runner's declarations then agree with the proofs'
   locations. The code block and the verdict are unchanged.
   Proved (fault freedom at the runner's declarations, MEMVALS):
   `SpinAbs.x64_spin_counter_envG_runner_faultFree`
   (Promising/SLR/EnvG/X64FaultFreeFixed.lean), with a `.Concrete` instance.
   Proved (LIVESPINX2): promise-free deadlock-freedom on a valid layout
   of the image (`[ValidLayout (layout spinImageV)]`):
   `Live.SpinX64XchgPF.spin_xchg_live_pf : XchgSpinLivePF fuel`, at the
   runner's layout `spin_xchg_live_pf_concrete` and from its start state
   `spin_xchg_live_pf_runnerN`; one-shot form `spin_xchg_live_oneShot_pf`
   (Promising/LiveSpinX64XchgPF.lean).
   Proved (LIVESPINXSEM2): deadlock-freedom with promises on the
   machine with semantic certification, every fuel, under `WeakFairSem ∧
   MemFair` (x86 `MemFair` is a modelling assumption):
   `Live.SpinX64SemXchgLive.spin_xchg_live_sem : XchgSpinLiveSem fuel`,
   `spin_xchg_live_sem_concrete`, `spin_xchg_live_sem_runnerN`; one-shot
   form `spin_xchg_live_oneShot_sem` (Promising/LiveSpinX64SemXchgLive.lean).
   The `XchgSpinLive` (over `succs`, incomplete `certify`) stays
   open (KNOWN_GAPS.md, "Liveness: spinlocks, x64 (LIVESPINX)").
# flags: -sym -fuel 300
# expect: Always
*)
{
uint32_t lock=0; uint32_t counter=0;
}
threads { P0: worker done; P1: worker done; }
code {
worker:
  movl (lock),%eax
  testl %eax,%eax
  jne worker
  movl $1,%eax
  xchgl %eax,(lock)
  testl %eax,%eax
  jne worker
  movl (counter),%ecx
  addl $1,%ecx
  movl %ecx,(counter)
  movl $0,(lock)
  jmp done
done:
}
forall [counter]=2
